		<meta property="schema:genre">Science Fiction</meta>
		<meta property="schema:genre">Shorts</meta>
		<dc:description id="description">A collection of short science fiction stories by Noel Loomis.</dc:description>
		<meta id="long-description" property="se:long-description" refines="#description">
			&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/noel-loomis"&gt;Noel Loomis&lt;/a&gt; was a prolific writer of short fiction for popular pulp magazines from the 1930s into the 1970s. While he wrote many western novels and some western short fiction, the majority of his short-form work was science fiction.&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;Loomis’s science fiction is distinct from many of his contemporaries in that his stories often imagined the future evolution of blue-collar professions. While he certainly wrote stories about space travel and futuristic military action as was common in his era, he also penned many that explore the future of everyday professions, including (and especially) his own professional background in as a linotype machine operator.&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;In Loomis’s body of science fiction work, readers will find the expected tales of futuristic war, time travel, and interplanetary exploration that one expects from pulp science fiction of the era; and between those stories, they will encounter others about futuristic parking garage logistics, personal injury litigation, and even bending laws of time and space to meet publishing deadlines.&lt;/p&gt;
		</meta>
		<dc:language>en-US</dc:language>
